{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I will bless:</b> This counsel was from Him at the outset, for He is the one who teaches man knowledge." "And the meaning of <b>in the nights</b> — when he isolates himself from the affairs of the world." "<b>And my kidneys:</b> an allusion to the generative faculties, which are hidden, like the kidneys." "And the meaning of <b>they admonished me</b> — that he pondered in his heart all that befalls those who depart from this world; therefore he was admonished." "<b>I have set:</b> Counsel and discipline brought him to set HaShem before him day and night. And behold, his soul is bound to its Creator before separation from its body. And because <b>I have set HaShem before me, at my right hand</b> — <b>I shall not be moved</b>, from the straight path."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:22.558952929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}